  "body": "This might be a bit of nitpicking, but- in the first two requirements, it seems a bit strange (to me) that you would have actual method/event-handler names when modeling the problem. I'm worried that this might restrict how the API looks in the end or might become confusing if the API ends up looking different than the requirement. \n\nI think it would be better to leave the API specific stuff to where the interfaces are defined... so: \n\n> - A `readStart` method that starts the flow of data\n> - A `readStop` method that sends an advisory signal to stop the flow of data\n> - A `ondata` handler that fires when new data is pushed from the source\n\nCould become something like:\n\n> - Some means that starts the flow of data\n> - Some means that sends an advisory signal to stop the flow of data\n> - An event handler that fires when new data is pushed from the source\n",
